# app: Neovim
# source: https://neo.vimhelp.org/quickref.txt.html#quickref
# source-raw: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/neovim/neovim/master/runtime/doc/quickref.txt
# adapter: vimhelp-quickref
# scope: builtin
# checked: 2026-10-29

## Motion: left-right
left/right | h/l
first character in the line | 0
first non-blank character in the line | ^
next EOL (end of line) position | $
first character in screen line (differs from "0" when lines wrap) | g0
first non-blank character in screen line (differs from "^" when lines wrap) | g^
last character in screen line (differs from "$" when lines wrap) | g$
middle of the screen line | gm
middle of the line | gM
column {n} | \|
{n}th occurrence of {char} to the right/left | f{char}/F{char}
till before the {n}th occurrence of {char} to the right/left | t{char}/T{char}
repeat the last "f", "F", "t", or "T" {n} times | ;
repeat the last "f", "F", "t", or "T" {n} times in opposite direction | ,

## Motion: up-down
up/down {n} lines | k/j
up/down {n} lines, on the first non-blank character | -/+
down {n}-1 lines, on the first non-blank character | _
go to line {n} (default: last/first line), on the first non-blank character | G/gg
go to line {n} percentage down in the file; {n} must be given, otherwise it is the % command | %
up {n} screen lines (differs from "k" when line wraps) | gk
down {n} screen lines (differs from "j" when line wraps) | gj

## Motion: text objects
{n} words forward/backward | w/b
{n} blank-separated WORDs forward/backward | W/B
forward/backward to the end of the {n}th word | e/ge
forward/backward to the end of the {n}th blank-separated WORD | E/gE
{n} sentences forward/backward | )/(
{n} paragraphs forward/backward | }/{
{n} sections forward/backward, at start of section | ]]/[[
{n} sections forward/backward, at end of section | ][/[]
{n} times back to unclosed '(' | [(
{n} times back to unclosed '{' | [{
{n} times back to start/end of method (for Java) | [m/[M
{n} times forward to unclosed ')' | ])
{n} times forward to unclosed '}' | ]}
{n} times forward to start/end of method (for Java) | ]m/]M
{n} times back to unclosed "#if" or "#else" | [#
{n} times forward to unclosed "#else" or "#endif" | ]#
{n} times back to start of comment "/*" | [*
{n} times forward to end of comment "*/" | ]*

## Search
search forward/backward for the {n}th occurrence of {pattern} | /{pattern}<CR> / ?{pattern}<CR>
repeat last search, in the forward/backward direction | / ?
repeat last search | n
repeat last search, in opposite direction | N
search forward/backward for the identifier under the cursor | */#
like "*", but also find partial matches | g*
like "#", but also find partial matches | g#
go to local declaration of identifier under the cursor | gd
go to global declaration of identifier under the cursor | gD

## Marks
mark current position with mark {a-zA-Z} | m{a-zA-Z}
go to mark {a-z} within current file | `{a-z}
go to mark {A-Z} in any file | `{A-Z}
go to the position where Vim was previously exited | `{0-9}
go to the position before the last jump | ``
go to the position when last editing this file | `"
go to the start/end of the previously operated or put text | `[/`]
go to the start/end of the (previous) Visual area | `</`>
go to the position of the last change in this file | `.
same as `, but on the first non-blank in the line | '{a-zA-Z0-9[]'"<>.}
go to {n}th older/newer position in jump list | C-o/C-i

## Motion: various
find the next brace, bracket, comment, or "#if"/ "#else"/"#endif" in this line and go to its match | %
go to the {n}th line in the window, on the first non-blank | H
go to the middle line in the window, on the first non-blank | M
go to the {n}th line from the bottom, on the first non-blank | L
go to {n}th byte in the buffer | go

## Tags
jump to the tag under cursor, unless changes have been made | C-]
jump back from {n}th older tag in tag list | C-t
like C-] but show tag in preview window | C-w }
close tag preview window | C-w z

## Scrolling
window {n} lines down/up | C-e/C-y
window {n} lines down/up (default: 1/2 window) | C-d/C-u
window {n} pages forward/backward | C-f/C-b
redraw, current line at top of window | z<CR>/zt
redraw, current line at center of window | z./zz
redraw, current line at bottom of window | z-/zb
scroll screen {n} characters to the right/left | zh/zl
scroll screen half a screenwidth to the right/left | zH/zL

## Insert: text
append text after the cursor | a
append text at the end of the line | A
insert text before the cursor | i
insert text before the first non-blank in the line | I
insert text in column 1 | gI
open a new line below/above the current line, append text | o/O

## Insert: text (Visual block)
insert the same text in front of all the selected lines | I
append the same text after all the selected lines | A

## Insert: keys (leaving)
end Insert mode, back to Normal mode | Esc
like Esc, but do not use an abbreviation | C-c
execute {command} and return to Insert mode | C-o {command}

## Insert: keys (moving)
move cursor left/right/up/down | Up/Dn/Lt/Rt
one word left/right | S-Lt/S-Rt
one screenful backward/forward | S-Up/S-Dn
cursor after last character in the line | End
cursor to first character in the line | Home

## Insert: special keys
insert character literally, or enter decimal byte value | C-v {char}..
begin new line | NL/CR/C-m/C-j
insert the character from below/above the cursor | C-e/C-y
insert previously inserted text | C-a
insert previously inserted text and stop Insert mode | C-@
insert next/previous match of identifier before the cursor | C-n/C-p
complete the word before the cursor in various ways | C-x ...
delete the character before the cursor | BS/C-h
delete the character under the cursor | Del
delete word before the cursor | C-w
delete all entered characters in the current line | C-u
insert one shiftwidth of indent in front of the current line | C-t
delete one shiftwidth of indent in front of the current line | C-d
delete all indent in the current line | 0 C-d
delete all indent in the current line, restore indent in next line | ^ C-d

## Delete
delete {n} characters under and after the cursor | x/Del
delete {n} characters before the cursor | X
delete the text that is moved over with {motion} | d{motion}
delete the highlighted text | {visual}d
delete {n} lines | dd
delete to the end of the line (and {n}-1 more lines) | D
join {n}-1 lines (delete <EOL>s) | J
join the highlighted lines | {visual}J
like "J", but without inserting spaces | gJ
like "{visual}J", but without inserting spaces | {visual}gJ

## Copy and move
use register {char} for the next delete, yank, or put | "{char}
yank the text moved over with {motion} into a register | y{motion}
yank the highlighted text into a register | {visual}y
yank {n} lines into a register | yy/Y
put a register after/before the cursor position | p/P
like p, but adjust indent to current line | ]p
like P, but adjust indent to current line | [p
like p, but leave cursor after the new text | gp
like P, but leave cursor after the new text | gP

## Change
replace {n} characters with {char} | r{char}
replace {n} characters without affecting layout | gr{char}
enter Replace mode (repeat the entered text {n} times) | R
enter virtual Replace mode - Like Replace mode but without affecting layout | gR
change the text that is moved over with {motion} | c{motion}
change the highlighted text | {visual}c
change {n} lines | cc/S
change to the end of the line (and {n}-1 more lines) | C
change {n} characters | s
switch case for {n} characters and advance cursor | ~
switch case for highlighted text | {visual}~
make highlighted text lowercase/uppercase | {visual}u/{visual}U
switch case for the text that is moved over with {motion} | g~{motion}
make the text that is moved over with {motion} lowercase/uppercase | gu{motion}/gU{motion}
perform rot13 encoding on the text that is moved over with {motion} | g?{motion}
add {n} to the number at or after the cursor | C-a
subtract {n} from the number at or after the cursor | C-x
move the lines that are moved over with {motion} one shiftwidth left/right | <{motion}/>{motion}
move {n} lines one shiftwidth left/right | <</>>
format the lines that are moved over with {motion} to 'textwidth' length | gq{motion}

## Change (Visual block)
replace each char of the selected text with {char} (change = delete text and enter Insert mode) | {visual}r{char}
change each of the selected lines with the entered text | {visual}c
change each of the selected lines until end-of-line with the entered text | {visual}C

## Change: complex
filter the lines that are moved over through {command} | !{motion}{command}<CR>
filter {n} lines through {command} | !!{command}<CR>
filter the highlighted lines through {command} | {visual}!{command}<CR>
filter the lines that are moved over through 'equalprg' | ={motion}
filter {n} lines through 'equalprg' | ==
filter the highlighted lines through 'equalprg' | {visual}=
repeat previous ":s" on current line without options | &

## Visual
start/stop char highlight | v
start/stop line highlight | V
start/stop block highlight | C-v
exchange cursor with selection start | o
reselect previous visual area | gv

## Text objects
select a word / inner word | aw/iw
select a WORD / inner WORD | aW/iW
select a sentence / inner sentence | as/is
select a paragraph / inner paragraph | ap/ip
select all lines | al
select "inner line" | il
select a block / inner block (from "[(" to "])") | ab/ib
select a Block / inner Block (from `[{` to `]}`) | aB/iB
select a <> block / inner <> block | a>/i>
select a tag block / inner tag block (from <aaa> to </aaa>) | at/it
select a single quoted string / inner single quoted string | a'/i'
select a double quoted string / inner double quoted string | a"/i"
select a backward quoted string / inner backward quoted string | a`/i`

## Repeat
repeat last change (with count replaced with {n}) | .
record typed characters into register {a-z} | q{a-z}
record typed characters, appended to register {a-z} | q{A-Z}
stop recording | q
replay last recorded macro | Q
execute the contents of register {a-z} | @{a-z}
repeat previous @{a-z} | @@
sleep for {n} seconds | gs

## Undo and redo
undo last {n} changes | u
redo last {n} undone changes | C-r
restore last changed line | U

## Various
clear and redraw the screen | C-l
show current file name (with path) and cursor position | C-g
show ascii value of character under cursor in decimal, hex, and octal | ga
for utf-8 encoding - show byte sequence for character under cursor in hex | g8
show cursor column, line, and character position | g C-g
during searches - Interrupt the search | C-c
while entering a count - delete last character | Del

## Command-line
abandon command-line (if 'wildchar' is Esc, type it twice) | Esc
insert {char} literally | C-v {char}
enter decimal value of character (up to three digits) | C-v {number}
enter digraph (see :digraphs) | C-k {char1} {char2}
insert the contents of a register | C-r {register}
cursor left/right | Lt/Rt
cursor to beginning/end of command-line | C-b/C-e
delete the character in front of the cursor | BS
delete the character under the cursor | Del
delete the word in front of the cursor | C-w
remove all characters between the cursor and beginning of command-line | C-u
recall older/newer command-line that starts with current command | Up/Dn
recall older/newer command-line from history | S-Up/S-Dn
next/previous match when 'incsearch' is active | C-g/C-t

## Command-line (completion)
list all names that match the pattern in front of the cursor | C-d
insert all names that match pattern in front of cursor | C-a
insert longest common part of names that match pattern | C-l
after 'wildchar' with multiple matches - go to next/previous match | C-n/C-p

## Write and quit
write if changed and quit (:x) | ZZ
quit without writing (:q!) | ZQ
suspend (or start a shell) | C-z

## Windows
split window into two parts (:split) | C-w s
split window and jump to tag under cursor | C-w ]
split window and edit file name under the cursor | C-w f
split window and edit alternate file | C-w ^
create new empty window (:new) | C-w n
quit editing and close window (:q[uit]) | C-w q
make buffer hidden and close window (:clo[se]) | C-w c
make current window only one on the screen (:on[ly]) | C-w o
move cursor to window below/above | C-w j/k
move cursor to window below/above (wrap) | C-w C-w/W
move cursor to top window | C-w t
move cursor to bottom window | C-w b
move cursor to previous active window | C-w p
rotate windows down/up | C-w r/R
exchange current window with next one | C-w x
make all windows equal height & width | C-w =
decrease/increase current window height | C-w -/+
set current window height | C-w _
decrease/increase current window width | C-w </>
set current window width | C-w \|

## Folding
operator - Define a fold manually | zf{motion}
delete one fold under the cursor | zd
delete all folds under the cursor | zD
open/close one fold under the cursor | zo/zc
open/close all folds under the cursor | zO/zC
fold more - decrease 'foldlevel' | zm
close all folds - make 'foldlevel' zero | zM
reduce folding - increase 'foldlevel' | zr
open all folds - make 'foldlevel' max | zR
fold none - reset 'foldenable' | zn
fold normal set 'foldenable' | zN
invert 'foldenable' | zi
